<title>AUSTRIA: NIGERIA SAYS NOT PRODUCING ABOVE OPEC QUOTA.</title>
<headline>NIGERIA SAYS NOT PRODUCING ABOVE OPEC QUOTA.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nigerian oil minister Dan Etete said on Tuesday his country was not producing above its OPEC assigned quota and so saw no need for it to reduce its output.  </p>
<p>Asked by reporters on his way to the three-man quota compliance committee meeting, to which Nigeria belongs, if Nigeria should cut back production he said: &quot;No, that is out of the question, I don't think so</p>
<p>&quot;For OPEC members who are producing it is logical for them to cut back,&quot; he added. &quot;Whatever we do will be for the best interests of OPEC and the market&quot;.</p>
<p>Iran's Gholamreza Aghazadeh, who is chairing the quota compliance committee meeting, made no comment to reporters on his way to the talks.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 713 2002</p>
